comments.body:
I don't have enough knowledge on this topic 😄.

@danielcuthbert and @unprovable, any idea on this?

@jedisct1, any perspective on this topic?

We can add AEGIS-128L and AEGIS-256 to the list of allowed AEAD.

Then there are a lot of remaining things mentioned in the IETF Draft:

* AEGIS-128X, AEGIS-256X;
* AEGIS as a Stream Cipher;
* AEGISMAC-128L, AEGISMAC-256, AEGISMAC-128X, AEGISMAC-256X.

I'm not sure if we need to include all of those.

@danielcuthbert, To clarify, is your comment about AEGIS in general or about the parallel modes only (AEGIS-128X and AEGIS-256X)?

* AEGIS-128L and AEGIS-256 are described in this [paper from 2016](https://competitions.cr.yp.to/round3/aegisv11.pdf), I guess they are pretty stable?
* AEGIS-128X and AEGIS-256X on the other hand are only described in the IETF draft.
